WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:02.958
(joyful music)

00:00:03.964 --> 00:00:06.668
- [Narrator] Snow means
something different to everyone.

00:00:06.668 --> 00:00:09.543
- Snow takes all the complicated details

00:00:09.543 --> 00:00:11.630
and simplifies the landscape toward

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:15.092
the possibilities of
naturally occurring sculpture.

00:00:15.092 --> 00:00:17.067
- [Narrator] For snow
globe artist Walter Martin

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:20.111
and Paloma Muñoz, snow
is what draws you into

00:00:20.111 --> 00:00:21.778
their surreal world.

00:00:23.205 --> 00:00:25.024
- There's like a paradise feeling

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:27.168
where man and beast live in peace

00:00:27.168 --> 00:00:30.183
and work together to do the laundry.

00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:31.950
- [Narrator] Here, they work out ambitions

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:33.852
and exercise anxiety.

00:00:33.852 --> 00:00:36.133
- Teetering, there's a sense of teetering

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.367
and of continuous balance.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:40.374
- [Narrator] The globes
freeze miniature landscapes

00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:42.221
in wintry wonder.

00:00:42.221 --> 00:00:43.304
Twisted logic

00:00:44.152 --> 00:00:46.320
and macabre humor.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.217
- It's like our own little form of poetry.

00:00:49.217 --> 00:00:51.457
- [Narrator] Inspired by
nature and the elements.

00:00:51.457 --> 00:00:53.991
- We feel a lot of angst and dread

00:00:53.991 --> 00:00:56.008
sometimes in the winter.

00:00:56.008 --> 00:01:00.036
And (whoosh) it goes into the globe.

00:01:00.036 --> 00:01:02.064
- [Narrator] The couple
puts a modern twist

00:01:02.064 --> 00:01:03.792
on an age old craft.

00:01:03.792 --> 00:01:07.959
Transforming nick knacks
into custom works of art.

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:14.623
- So imagine a world full of stories

00:01:14.623 --> 00:01:17.535
and the camera goes in and just picks up

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:21.615
this little fragment in
time and a little moment.

00:01:21.615 --> 00:01:23.286
That's what the globes are.

00:01:23.286 --> 00:01:26.119
They're samples of a larger world,

00:01:27.227 --> 00:01:30.227
but becomes alive when you shake it.

00:01:31.505 --> 00:01:34.088
(joyful music)

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:44.201
Working together for us is one experiment.

00:01:44.201 --> 00:01:46.909
Maybe like a marriage, but
it's a more complex marriage

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:50.017
because we're trying
to create art together.

00:01:50.017 --> 00:01:54.184
We've been doing the snow
globes now for almost 15 years.

00:01:57.219 --> 00:01:58.789
We started in 2001.

00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:01.126
That was when we made the first one

00:02:01.126 --> 00:02:04.876
and we had no idea we
were going to be making

00:02:04.876 --> 00:02:07.126
snow globes 15 years later.

00:02:19.219 --> 00:02:21.485
Everything starts with a small canvas that

00:02:21.485 --> 00:02:25.612
is the space that you
have to fill in the globe.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:28.831
And then, you start adding figures

00:02:28.831 --> 00:02:31.208
and you continue to
explore their landscape

00:02:31.208 --> 00:02:34.327
in relationship to those figures.

00:02:34.327 --> 00:02:36.708
- I think I was fascinated with the way

00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:40.159
that the snow kind of takes all
the complicated details

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.404
and simplifies the landscape,

00:02:42.404 --> 00:02:44.817
the unification of the landscape.

00:02:44.817 --> 00:02:47.472
It tends to be a great equalizer.

00:02:47.472 --> 00:02:50.161
And when there's something
outside of that world

00:02:50.161 --> 00:02:52.250
that's interjected into it, like a human

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:56.936
with a colorful wardrobe, or
an animal, or a small house,

00:02:56.936 --> 00:02:59.711
or anything that's not of that world,

00:02:59.711 --> 00:03:01.382
becomes the focus.

00:03:01.382 --> 00:03:03.132
It is a frozen world.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:12.877
- [Paloma] We live at
the edge of a small town

00:03:12.877 --> 00:03:14.808
and on the other side of our house

00:03:14.808 --> 00:03:18.229
is North Eastern American Forest.

00:03:18.229 --> 00:03:22.816
It's complete wilderness
and we walk it everyday

00:03:22.816 --> 00:03:24.621
and we love it.

00:03:24.621 --> 00:03:27.393
- [Walter] Depending on what
day and the time of year

00:03:27.393 --> 00:03:29.119
and the time of day and the weather,

00:03:29.119 --> 00:03:32.802
uh, the forest can offer
a totally different face.

00:03:32.802 --> 00:03:35.066
- It's like we have one
foot in the wilderness

00:03:35.066 --> 00:03:37.631
and one foot in civilization.

00:03:37.631 --> 00:03:41.798
We can bring those worlds
together through our work.

00:03:46.113 --> 00:03:48.747
We see a lot of silly
things throughout the day.

00:03:48.747 --> 00:03:50.830
It leeches into the work.

00:03:59.621 --> 00:04:01.278
- I'm from Northern Virginia,

00:04:01.278 --> 00:04:05.034
which is a flat coastal
city in mid-atlantic region

00:04:05.034 --> 00:04:08.390
not known for it's snow storms.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.931
So I fantasized about escaping to a place

00:04:10.931 --> 00:04:12.641
where there was snow.

00:04:12.641 --> 00:04:14.963
- For me, the challenge is always

00:04:14.963 --> 00:04:17.216
how to make something that is relevant

00:04:17.216 --> 00:04:21.479
that contributes something
to the conversation

00:04:21.479 --> 00:04:25.415
of what art is and what
being a human-being in this

00:04:25.415 --> 00:04:27.332
moment in time is like.

00:04:29.573 --> 00:04:33.060
- [Walter] A successful snow
globe would be absurdist humor

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.143
combined with a real human condition.

00:04:37.404 --> 00:04:40.057
- I think people find the
globes very interesting.

00:04:40.057 --> 00:04:41.075
They love them.

00:04:41.075 --> 00:04:44.081
They absorb you and they allow the viewer

00:04:44.081 --> 00:04:47.948
to be immersed even for just a few seconds

00:04:47.948 --> 00:04:51.414
in a completely different world.

00:04:51.414 --> 00:04:53.997
(joyful music)

